// NOTE: When I return to this, it's worth breaking up a yarn project for each "chapter" of the game.
// We can use this namespacing convention epending on the phases of that chapter, since it may not be consistent across chapters

// title: Brewing_Chapter2
// ---
// // Declare these in the main file, weird to have in one chapter but not the other
// // <<declare $is_served = false>>
// // <<declare $is_pref = true>>
// ===

title: Brewing_Chapter2_OldMan
---
<<if $is_served == false>>
    Old Man: It's been difficult out there... You've been holding up great, but I fear the lack of supplies will force important decisions upon our selves.
    Old Man: I hope you're holding up, I've definitely been holding on to the stress myself
<<elseif $is_served == true and $is_pref == true>>
    Old Man: This will help me relax, thank you! Save the good stuff for others.
    Old Man: Should more injured come by, don't forget that White Tea heals wounds and ailments most effectively!
<<else>>
    Old Man: Really make sure to listen to the needs of your customers, above all else.
    Old Man: And make choices that align with who... you... are...
<<endif>>
===

title: Brewing_Chapter2_General
---
<<if $is_served == false>>
    General: It's been years, Tea Seller... I hope you take it upon yourself to do the right thing and aid the soldiers that come through here.
<<elseif $is_served == true and $is_pref == true>>
    General: Thank you, once again!
    General: Should you prove to be an important aid to our soldiers, the military will surely reward you after our decisive victory, Tea Seller.
<<else>>
    General: It would be wise of you to prioritize those fighting for your fief...
    General: The military recognizes those who sacrifice for the greate good of the people.
<<endif>>
===

title: Brewing_Chapter2_SoldierFine1
---
<<if $is_served == false>>
    Soldier: I missed breakfast this morning, please give me something that'll energize me!
<<elseif $is_served == true and $is_pref == true>>
    Soldier: This is amazing, almost better than the potions we packed!
<<else>>
    Soldier: Gah, I wish we packed more potions...
<<endif>>
===

title: Brewing_Chapter2_SoldierHurt1
---
<<if $is_served == false>>
    Hurt Soldier: My arm... I need something to help me heal it...
<<elseif $is_served == true and $is_pref == true>>
    Hurt Soldier: Wow, I feel an energetic buzz! The pain is ebbing!
<<else>>
    Hurt Soldier: Well, I suppose this will distract me
<<endif>>
===

title: Brewing_Chapter2_SoldierHurt2
---
<<if $is_served == false>>
    Hurt Soldier: My leg... I need something to help me heal it...
<<elseif $is_served == true and $is_pref == true>>
    Hurt Soldier: Wow, I feel an energetic buzz! The pain is ebbing!
<<else>>
    Hurt Soldier: Well, I suppose this will distract me
<<endif>>
===

title: Brewing_Chapter2_SoldierFine2
---
<<if $is_served == false>>
    Soldier: I've been on a roll today but feel rather tired, give me something to last a longer time on the battlefield!
<<elseif $is_served == true and $is_pref == true>>
    Soldier: This is the stuff! The General knows his tea
<<else>>
    Soldier: This... isn't what I smelled the General having... but I'll try it anyway
<<endif>>
===

title: Brewing_Chapter2_SoldierHurt3
---
<<if $is_served == false>>
    Hurt Soldier: My neck... I need something to help me heal it...
<<elseif $is_served == true and $is_pref == true>>
    Hurt Soldier: Wow, I feel an energetic buzz! The pain is ebbing!
<<else>>
    Hurt Soldier: Well, I suppose this will distract me
<<endif>>
===

title: Brewing_Chapter2_Forg
---
<<if $is_served == false>>
    Forg: Merk, HELP!!!! I've been tasked with delivering a crucial message to the frontier lines, but I've injured my leg.
    Forg: I know I can rely on you for brewing something to help me accomplish it!
<<elseif $is_served == true and $is_pref == true>>
    Forg: Once again, the effect is immediate! I always know you have my back.
<<else>>
    Forg: Hmm, I know this isn't it. I guess I'll have to look elsewhere, or push myself on this injury...
<<endif>>
===

title: Brewing_Chapter2_SketchyFarmer
---
<<if $is_served == false>>
    Sketchy Farmer: It's interesting what one choice, made with knowledge or without, can change like a butterfly flapping its wings.
    Sketchy Farmer: Personally, I like Lemon Ginger.
<<elseif $is_served == true and $is_pref == true>>
    Sketchy Farmer: Bold of you to assume the truth, or was this simply all that was left anyway?
<<else>>
    Sketchy Farmer: No one is ever truly up front, but did you think I was lying? Was this malicious?
    Sketchy Farmer: Or did you just incidentally serve the only tea bag you had of Lemon Ginger?
<<endif>>
===

